# 0. A hand-maintained release-drafter.yml, pre-dating this feature, must survive a
#    ciGenerateGithubWorkflow run while ciEnableReleaseDrafter is still at its default false -
#    regression test for a bug where the disabled branch deleted it unconditionally.
> writeHandMaintainedWorkflow
> ciGenerateGithubWorkflow
> checkWorkflowHandMaintainedPreserved

# 1. false -> true: enabling generates the workflow and scaffolds the config.
> set ThisBuild / ciEnableReleaseDrafter := true
> ciGenerateGithubWorkflow
> checkWorkflowExists
> checkConfigExists

# 2. Hand-edit the config, then regenerate: content must NOT be overwritten (decision 5).
> handEditConfig
> ciGenerateGithubWorkflow
> checkConfigHandEditPreserved

# 3. Change a category setting, then regenerate: still no effect on the existing config file.
> set ThisBuild / ciReleaseDrafterCategories := Seq(zio.sbt.githubactions.ReleaseDrafterCategory("Changed", Seq("x")))
> ciGenerateGithubWorkflow
> checkConfigHandEditPreserved

# 4. true -> false: disabling deletes the workflow file...
> set ThisBuild / ciEnableReleaseDrafter := false
> ciGenerateGithubWorkflow
> checkWorkflowAbsent

# ...but leaves the hand-edited config alone.
> checkConfigHandEditPreserved

# 5. false -> true again: re-enabling regenerates the workflow, but still does not touch the
#    existing (hand-edited) config.
> set ThisBuild / ciEnableReleaseDrafter := true
> ciGenerateGithubWorkflow
> checkWorkflowExists
> checkConfigHandEditPreserved
